<h3>Guild Structure Overview<o:p></o:p></h3>

<h4>Ranks, Roles, and Honorary Titles<o:p></o:p></h4>

<p>Ranks are positions that form the command structure within the guild. The
commanding ranks are Warlord, Circle of Bones, Blood Knight, and Bone Guard. Command
ranking members are responsible for the overall management of the guild. They
handle both internal and external guild issues, work on public relations, and
provide the infrastructure necessary for guild management. Members are
appointed to the various ranks by the Circle of Bones.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Roles are specialized positions that are separate from the chain of command.
These are specific jobs that various members carry out so that the Ranking
members can focus on overall guild management, while the members that fill a
role do not need to worry about anything except their assigned role. Although
roles are not a ranking position, they are indeed a very important part of the
guild and command the same respect as a member of rank. Members are appointed
to the various roles by the Circle of Bones.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Honorary Titles are given to members by the Circle of Bones based on merit,
honor, and ability. We often have so many good members that we do not have
enough ranks or positions to promote everybody as a way of recognizing their
contributions to the guild. In cases like this, the Circle of Bones may decide
to bestow an Honorary Title upon a member. It should be noted that an Honorary
Title is a great reward. Anybody with an Honorary Title is recognized as a
significant contributor to the guild and should be treated with the same
respect as a member of rank.<o:p></o:p></p>

